This beautifully presented four bedroom family home offers spacious and versatile accommodation arranged over three floors, combining charming character features with modern living.
Upon entering the property, you are welcomed by a bright entrance hall leading into a large open plan living and dining room. This impressive space features a modern fireplace and distinctive Tudor style windows, creating a warm and inviting atmosphere ideal for both everyday living and entertaining.
To the rear of the property is a newly refurbished kitchen, thoughtfully designed with a large central island positioned beneath a skylight, allowing natural light to flood the space. The kitchen also benefits from integrated appliances and bi-folding doors that open directly onto the garden, seamlessly connecting indoor and outdoor living.
The ground floor further benefits from a dedicated home office area, perfect for remote working, as well as a convenient downstairs W/C.
The first floor comprises two generous double bedrooms, both featuring built in wardrobes, along with a third bedroom currently used as a walk in wardrobe. A newly refurbished family bathroom completes this level.
Occupying the entire top floor is the impressive master suite, offering a private retreat with its own en-suite shower room.
Externally, the property boasts a well maintained rear garden, which backs onto the Inwood Bird Sanctuary, with a large patio area, ideal for enjoying sunny days and outdoor dining, while the remainer is mainly laid to lawn. At the rear of the garden there is also a useful outbuilding, currently used as a workshop, ideal for a studio, working area or gym.
To the front of the property, a paved driveway provides off street parking for two vehicles.
LOCATION
Court Avenue is a quiet residential road, consisting of mock Tudor period family homes.
Old Coulsdon is an affluent area with exemplary schools and a local college.
The property is exceptionally well connected to regular bus services (including routes directly to the local train station providing access for commuters into London Bridge and London Victoria)
You are just a short stroll from a vibrant parade of local amenities including a GP surgery, post office, bakery and an award winning curry house. The landmark Tudor Rose Public House is a perfect spot for a quiet drink, meals and Sunday roasts.
For those who enjoy the outdoors, you are spoilt for choice with vast green open spaces nearby. Coulsdon Common and Happy Valley are ideal for dog friendly or leisurely walks, whilst the local park features a café during the day.
Coulsdon Town Centre is a 5 minute drive away, offering an array of shops, cafes and restaurants.
