Accommodation comprises a spacious entrance hall leading into the front aspect reception room with ample space for relaxing and entertaining and double doors through to the large conservatory with garden views. A further dining room with front aspect bay offers excellent additional space. To the rear of the property, the well equipped kitchen comprises a quality range of high gloss wall and base units with work surfaces and breakfast bar area, incorporating inset sink unit, induction hob with inbuilt extractor, wall mounted oven, and further integrated appliances. A separate utility room offers additional work and appliance space. The kitchen opens through to a further lounge with doors onto the garden. To the first floor, there are five well proportioned bedrooms – one en-suite - plus a family bathroom with luxury bath suite and separate shower unit. A delightful bonus mezzanine area provides versatile living space.

The property is located within easy access of Tramlink from Lloyd Park, as well as South Croydon station, providing convenient links into East Croydon station and Central London. Regular bus routes also link nearby Croydon town centre with its array of shops and amenities, and the area is also well served by excellent schools.', 'Marriott Vernon, Croydon and surrounding areas', '2026-03-21T16:00:34Z', '2026-10-24T10:08:19Z', '[]', 'train');
The property is set in a commanding position on the road and immediately impresses with its attractive appearance and welcoming feel. An enclosed entrance porch opens into the charming reception hall, setting the tone for the character and period detail found throughout. The sitting room is a particularly elegant space, wonderfully light and airy, with two windows to the front, a beautiful feature fireplace with wooden mantel surround, and double doors opening onto the delightful loggia – a lovely place to sit and enjoy the outlook.
The dining room is equally impressive and ideal for both family meals and entertaining, featuring a striking curved bay window to the front and a characterful fireplace with tiled inset. In addition, there is a versatile study/reception room, a bright double aspect room with a window to the side and views over the rear garden, together with fitted shelving to either side, making it perfect for home working, reading or an additional family space. A useful downstairs WC/cloakroom adds everyday convenience.
To the rear of the house, the superb kitchen/family room provides a wonderful hub of the home. Beautifully arranged with a full range of fitted units, it includes a built-in oven and grill, five-ring gas hob with stainless steel extractor above, integrated dishwasher and fridge, and ample workspace for busy family life. Two sets of bi-fold doors open directly onto the rear garden, creating a seamless connection between inside and out and making this an ideal space for entertaining during the warmer months. A separate utility room provides additional practicality, with space and plumbing for a washing machine.
Upstairs, the property continues to impress with four well-proportioned and beautifully light bedrooms. The principal bedroom enjoys a front aspect and is fitted with a range of wardrobes, together with an en-suite shower room featuring a shower cubicle and fitted cupboards. A further double bedroom to the front also benefits from windows to both the front and side, along with fitted wardrobes. Another double bedroom is double aspect, with windows to the side and rear, while the fourth double bedroom overlooks the rear garden. The family bathroom is well appointed with both a bath and separate shower cubicle.
Outside, the rear garden is a real feature of the home – mature, secluded and beautifully established, offering a wonderful space for relaxing, playing or entertaining. Immediately outside of the house is a large patio area with a further circular patio which provides an ideal seating area, with mature shrubs and trees creating a lovely sense of privacy. There is also a wooden shed and gated side access. To the front, the property benefits from an attached double garage with electric up-and-over door, a brick herringbone-style driveway, and an area of lawn completing the attractive approach.
Altogether, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a charming Edwardian family home in one of Purley’s most desirable roads.
My House My Home.
“We have had thirty incredibly happy years living in, updating, and maintaining in good order our home “Cawsworth”
We moved in over 30 years ago with our young family, who have grown up and blossomed enjoying the spacious, quality environment that a house built in the early 1900’s in a generous broad plot gives.
Moving to this easy to run house allowed us to use the well respected local schools that are a walk or short drive away.
Cawsworth has always been a great home for entertaining which, when the weather permits, allows guests to spill on to the terraces and into the garden.
Popular with the children and their friends when young, providing space for a marquee at weddings, birthdays and family occasions, the easily maintained, secluded, quiet and safe garden is a haven.
With parking for many cars, the driveway allows easy unloading of shopping and luggage at the front door, and the large, secure double garage has stored valuable cars without worry.
We have enjoyed the fact that Cawsworth is just a short walk from Purley or Coulsdon South station with immediate links to central London. By road, the M23 / M25 is less than 15 minutes away and gives excellent access to the national road network, airports, the coast, and the countryside.
Manor Way is also very neighbourly which has been a constant comfort for us. We shall be sad to leave Cawsworth and the many friends we have made in the street, but we are sure new residents will be warmly welcomed and we hope this lovely home will provide for a new family as much happiness as we have had here”
