INSIDE

Entered on the fifth floor, the apartment opens into a striking open-plan living, dining and kitchen space arranged around expansive triple glazing and direct access to a private balcony with panoramic London views. Oak flooring with underfloor heating runs throughout, while distinct living and dining zones create a layout equally suited to everyday living and entertaining.

The kitchen is sleek and architectural in feel, centred around matte airbrushed cabinetry and fully integrated Smeg appliances. Further thoughtful additions include a reverse osmosis drinking water system and a whole-home soft water system connected to all outlets and appliances. A generous guest WC and separate utility cupboard complete this level.

A sculptural balustraded staircase leads down to the bedroom floor, where custom Luxaflex thermal blackout blinds and natural fibre carpets introduce a softer, quieter material palette. The principal suite is particularly impressive, featuring a bespoke LEMMA Italian walk-in wardrobe and a luxurious en-suite bathroom with double shower and separate full-sized bath.

The second bedroom is also an excellent double, extending to approximately 167 sq ft, with its own en-suite shower room and access to a substantial under-stairs storage cupboard.

The building has a concierge, secure entry system, as well as a beautifully maintained communal garden, bicycle storage for residents and an exercise room.

