The airy reception hall with its stairway and cloakroom opens to a front-facing family room with a square walk-in bay window, a cast iron fireplace with wood surround and an adjacent drawing room with French doors opening directly to the sun terrace. The sizeable kitchen and dining space is filled with natural light via a second bay window and has a part glazed door opening to the sunny garden. There is ample space for dining, whilst the kitchen itself features a wide selection of glossy contemporary cabinetry with rich wooden work surfaces and a wealth of modern integrated appliances.

On the first floor is a family bathroom and four bright bedrooms, two of which enjoy feature fireplaces, with one benefitting from the front-facing bay. The second floor is home to the generous principal suite, which opens to a fully fitted walk-in wardrobe flowing into a sleek en suite shower room.

The property has a fine frontage approached via a brick-laid driveway, beside which is a plethora of mature and colourful shrubs. A paved pathway leads through to the storm porch with its pretty archway. The rear garden enjoys a paved sun terrace with a warm westerly aspect ideal for al fresco dining. This is followed by a lush level lawn enclosed with fencing and surrounded by established trees, shrubs and boBrders.

The thriving town of Sevenoaks benefits from a wide range of shopping and recreational facilities, including restaurants, bars, a theatre, library, cinema and various supermarkets, including a Waitrose. Sporting amenities nearby include golf at Knole Park and Wildernesse, a cricket ground at the Vine, tennis at Hollybush and a leisure centre. The mainline railway station offers fast and frequent services to London in just over half an hour and to Ashford International in under an hour. The M25 provides access to the motorway network, central London and the scenic Kent coastline. Renowned independent schools include Solefield, Sevenoaks Prep, Walthamstow Hall, The Granville and The New Beacon.', 'Strutt & Parker, Sevenoaks', '2026-06-08T15:51:26Z', '2026-10-24T10:17:42Z', '["floor_level"]', 'train');

