Arranged over three floors, this modern property provides superb access to highly regarded local schools, as well as Summertown, Wolvercote, and nearby road and rail links.

The ground floor features a bright and expansive reception room overlooking the rear garden, a wonderful space for family living and entertaining. This versatile room can easily accommodate both living and dining areas, complemented by an additional kitchen/dining space with room for a dining table.

On the first floor the property offers two double bedrooms and a single bedroom/study, providing flexibility for a family or those working from home. There is one en-suite bathroom and a family bathroom on this floor. The second floor provides two further double bedrooms, both of which benefit from en suite''s.

The decor throughout is light, neutral, and modern, creating a fresh and inviting atmosphere.

Situated within a quiet and secure gated community, the development offers privacy and peace of mind in a highly desirable part of Oxford.

Wolvercote is a sought after North Oxford suburb less than three miles from the city centre. With its riverside setting and village charm, it’s particularly popular with families and those seeking a balance between city convenience and a more relaxed lifestyle. The village offers a local shop, primary school, and several renowned gastro pubs. Excellent transport links include frequent buses to Oxford and regular trains to London Marylebone from Oxford Parkway (approximately two miles away).

North Oxford itself is one of the city’s most desirable residential areas, encompassing Jericho, Summertown, Wolvercote, and Cutteslowe. The area is renowned for its independent schools such as The Dragon School, Summer Fields, St Edward’s, and Oxford High School for Girls, as well as its close ties to the University of Oxford.

Port Meadow is within easy reach, offering beautiful walks along the Thames towards the city. There is also a bus stop adjacent to the development providing regular services to Oxford city centre.

Please note: Certain areas of Oxford are subject to a congestion charge of £5. Please check the website below before driving to your viewing to confirm whether your journey will cross a charging location. For further details, visit the Oxfordshire County Council website.', 'John D Wood & Co. Sales, Oxford', '2026-06-09T15:06:01Z', '2026-10-24T10:14:28Z', '["floor_level"]', 'train');
