Upon entering the property, you are welcomed by two well proportioned double bedrooms, including the principal suite. Both rooms benefit from excellent built in storage and an abundance of natural light. The principal bedroom is further enhanced by a stylish en suite bathroom, complete with a walk in shower. To the rear of this floor is the third double bedroom, a bright and spacious room that enjoys excellent natural light and features its own walk through wardrobe, adding practicality. A family bathroom is also located on this level, fitted with both a bathtub and a walk in shower.

Occupying the upper level is the stunning open plan kitchen and reception room, a beautifully light filled space designed for modern living. The kitchen benefits from three large skylights, which create a warm and airy atmosphere, and is finished with elegant white marble worktops and integrated appliances, giving a sleek and contemporary feel. The reception area is exceptionally bright, with near floor to ceiling terrace doors leading directly onto the private roof terrace. This wonderful outdoor space provides the perfect setting for socialising, entertaining, or relaxing during the warmer months.

Location

East Hill is in a superb location within Wandsworth. The area is renowned for its excellent local amenities, including the vibrant shops, cafes, and restaurants along St. John''s Hill and Old York Road, both approximately 0.3 miles away.

The expanses of Wandsworth Common are 1.0 miles away, providing open green spaces ideal for leisure and recreation. Commuters benefit from the proximity of Wandsworth Town mainline station, situated about 0.3 miles away offering regular services to London Waterloo. Additionally, numerous bus routes serve the area, enhancing connectivity to various parts of London.

Families are well-catered for, with a selection of reputable schools in the vicinity, both state and private. Notably, Allfarthing Primary School is conveniently located approximately 0.4 miles distance.

All distances are approximate, and sourced from Google Maps.

Leasehold with approximately 116 years remaining.', 'Savills, Wandsworth', '2026-06-12T15:39:02Z', '2026-10-23T23:03:41Z', '["epc_current"]', 'train');

Situated in an exceptionally well-connected location, this attractive and extended three-bedroom semi-detached home offers versatile family accommodation, an expansive rear garden with a dedicated home office, a garage, and ample driveway parking.

Ground Floor
The welcoming entrance hall leads into a generous bay-fronted living room, flooded with natural light. To the rear, the open-plan kitchen and breakfast room provides an ideal setting for family dining and entertaining. Adjoining the kitchen is a bright conservatory equipped with underfloor heating and bi-fold doors that open seamlessly onto the patio. A separate utility room and a cloakroom/WC provide everyday practicality.

First Floor
Upstairs features three well-proportioned bedrooms and a contemporary family bathroom. The two principal bedrooms benefit from extensive fitted storage solutions. The loft space is insulated and partially boarded, offering convenient ancillary storage.

Garden Studio & Outside Space
The split-level rear garden offers distinct areas for outdoor dining and entertaining. Positioned at the far end of the garden is a substantial, fully insulated detached garden studio. Complete with mains electricity and hardwired Ethernet connectivity, this building provides a turnkey remote-working environment, creative space, or garden retreat suitable for year-round use.

To the front, a private driveway provides off-road parking alongside an attached single garage with power and lighting.

Energy Efficiency & Technology
Installed in October 2025 and fully owned (included in the sale), the property features a state-of-the-art renewable energy setup:

14x 450 W solar panels (6.3 kW array)

Dual Tesla Powerwall 3 batteries offering 27 kWh of storage

Whole-home electric backup protection

Between March and September 2026 alone, the system generated over 5,100 kWh of clean electricity. This substantially cuts grid reliance, provides energy security, and produces passive income through surplus export tariffs.

Additional Features & Location
A whole-home water softener system is included, protecting internal plumbing, prolonging the lifespan of domestic appliances, and virtually eliminating limescale.

The property is exceptionally well-placed for transport and local amenities:

M4 (Junction 12): ~0.8 miles

Calcot Retail Park: 0.8 miles (IKEA, Sainsbury’s Savacentre)

Theale Railway Station: ~1.9 miles (direct links to Reading and London Paddington)

Services: Mains gas, electricity, water, and drainage. Gas central heating.

Renewable Energy: 14-panel solar array with twin Tesla Powerwall 3 batteries (fully owned; included in sale).

Water Treatment: Whole-home water softener (included in sale).

Local Authority: West Berkshire Council

Council Tax: Band C (£2,089.54 for current tax year, subject to confirmation)

The above information may be subject to change during the transaction period

