A beautifully presented one bedroom apartment situated within the prestigious Heron development.

Extending to approximately 566 sq ft, the apartment offers a well balanced layout comprising a spacious open plan reception room and contemporary kitchen, generous bedroom with fitted wardrobes, and a luxurious bathroom finished to a high specification. Floor to ceiling glazing floods the apartment with natural light.

The kitchen is fitted with premium integrated appliances and sleek cabinetry, while the bathroom features quality stone finishes and underfloor heating. The apartment also benefits from comfort cooling, integrated ceiling speakers and smart home technology.

Residents of The Heron enjoy access to an exceptional range of lifestyle facilities, including a 24-hour concierge, residents'' gym, exclusive club lounge, private dining and meeting rooms, cinema/screening room, business suite, bar and café, together with a landscaped rooftop garden offering a tranquil retreat above the City.

Location

The Heron enjoys a prime position in the heart of the City of London, surrounded by an outstanding selection of restaurants, cafés and lifestyle amenities. Popular dining destinations include The Ivy City Garden (0.3m), Hawksmoor Guildhall (0.2m), Sushi Samba (0.5m), Duck & Waffle (0.5m) and Eataly London (0.5m). For everyday convenience, Waitrose Moorgate (0.2m), Marks & Spencer Foodhall (0.2m) and One New Change Shopping Centre (0.6m) are all nearby.

Residents are also within easy reach of the cultural attractions of the Barbican Centre (0.2m), the Museum of London site (0.4m) and St Paul''s Cathedral (0.6m). Green open spaces can be found at Finsbury Circus Gardens (0.3m) and Postman''s Park (0.4m).

Transport links are exceptional, with Moorgate Station (0.1m), Barbican Station (0.3m), Liverpool Street Station (0.5m), Bank Station (0.5m) and Farringdon Station (0.7m) providing access across London and beyond. The development itself benefits from a 24-hour concierge, residents'' gym, cinema room, club lounge and rooftop garden.

