Property A - Originally built for storing ice during the 19th century, this unique one-bedroom property has been converted into a charming period house, complete with its own private courtyard. Enter a double-height reception room, where original stone walls, exposed timber beams and full-length glazing combine to create a striking, spacious and light-filled living space. There is a tiled fitted kitchen with gas appliances. Upstairs, an impressive mezzanine level leads to a generous double bedroom with fitted wardrobes, and a bathroom. The vaulted ceiling, exposed beams and skylights continue to showcase the building''s original character.
Apartment B -The studio apartment benefits from a private entrance, high ceilings, and large original windows, creating a bright, airy, and welcoming atmosphere throughout. The main living area provides ample space for comfortable studio-style living, with room to accommodate a dining area and a double bed. A few steps provide a subtle separation between the living space and the kitchen and bathroom, helping to create defined areas within the open layout.
Apartment C - A distinctive one-bedroom apartment. At the heart of the apartment is the impressive reception room with ceilings of over four metres and full-height, double-glazed bay windows. The exceptional proportions and abundance of natural light create a wonderfully bright living space. The reception room flows naturally into the adjoining kitchen. An additional feature is the stunning wrought-iron spiral staircase, which leads to a mezzanine level, which could be used as a home office, reading room or occasional sleeping accommodation. There is a practical fully tiled shower room.
The freehold is available for all three properties previously achieving £4550 per month rental, with the service charge split between the three properties and organised collectively.
Location
