There are many reasons we have loved this house as our first family home. Being in the school catchment for highly rated schools was our priority when we first moved. Now that we have two young children, we have seen how our location has benefitted them, not only getting into our desired school but also with their friends being so close by. As a family, we appreciate the lovely parks that are a short walking distance, each offering something different to our days out. Having restaurants, cafes and shops on our doorstep has meant that everything we need is easily accessible. Being a family that enjoy our holidays, we love the convenience of being able to get to Heathrow Airport in only half an hour.

We think our house has many features that have made it a great place to live. Firstly, having off street parking has been a huge bonus for the area. Having three double bedrooms has given us the space for our family to grow. Finally, we have ground floor aircon installed which has been invaluable to us, especially during the latest heatwaves.

We are lucky to be surrounded by kind and friendly neighbours who are always happy to help. It has been a great home for our family and a fantastic place to live.

Why we would buy it:

Combining contemporary elegance with practical design, this turnkey home requires no work and is ready for immediate enjoyment. The principal reception room creates an impressive backdrop for entertaining, showcased by striking exposed brickwork and built-in air conditioning. This main living area flows seamlessly into a modern, semi-separate kitchen, allowing for effort-free meal prep while keeping the chef fully connected to the home''s primary gathering space! The ground floor also benefits from a guest WC and additional room, ideal as a dedicated home office, utility room, cozy reading retreat, or children’s playroom.

The upper floors are thoughtfully arranged to accommodate growing families or hosting guests, featuring three genuine, well-proportioned double bedrooms and two sleek bathrooms. Stepping outside, the home opens up to a lovely private south-facing garden. Acting as a natural sun-drenched extension of the interior living space, this secluded outdoor haven is perfect for summer barbecues, alfresco dining, or simply relaxing in the afternoon sun.

Location is everything, and this residence puts the best of Northfields right on your doorstep. Nature lovers will appreciate being just a stone''s throw from the gates of the sprawling, green expanse of Lammas Park, while families gain the huge benefit of falling within the highly coveted Fielding Primary School catchment area. For daily convenience and evening leisure, a very short stroll brings you directly to Northfields Avenue, where a thriving, eclectic parade of independent cafes, local boutique shops, and global restaurants awaits.', 'Leslie & Co, West London', '2026-09-03T13:01:01Z', '2026-10-23T23:11:42Z', '[]', 'train');

Description

This striking three-storey family home offers almost 1,900 sq ft of stylish accommodation, combining modern functionality with elegant design. The property, built by reputable developers Hill in 2016, enjoys an attractive brick façade, a large garage, and a landscaped rear garden, all set within a peaceful, traffic-free residential area just over two miles from the historic Cambridge city centre.

Inside, the ground floor features an impressive open-plan kitchen/dining/family room, fitted with sleek cabinetry, stone worktops, an island with breakfast bar, integrated appliances including an induction hob, double oven (including a combi-oven), fridge and freezer, as well as ambient lighting. The current owners have added a bespoke pantry cupboard to provide further storage and further convenience. Bifold doors and large windows allow natural light to flood the space while connecting seamlessly with the garden—ideal for entertaining and family life. Also on the ground floor is a cloakroom/WC and utility area. The property also benefits from wooden shutters fitted to the windows for privacy throughout.

To the first floor, a spacious landing with large storage cupboards leads to a bright and airy sitting room with floor-to-ceiling windows. A generous double bedroom with fitted wardrobes and an en-suite shower room completes this level.

All floors have Amtico flooring and the ground and first have the added benefit of underfloor heating.

The top floor comprises three further well-proportioned bedrooms, including the luxurious principal suite with built-in storage and its own en-suite bathroom. A stylish family bathroom with a bath and a shower overhead serves the remaining bedrooms, and a large cupboard provides practical storage.

Outside, the landscaped garden is laid mostly to lawn with a paved terrace and fenced boundaries, offering privacy and a peaceful retreat. To the rear is access to the garage which provides off-street parking.

The property is being sold with no upward chain.

Location

Knightly Avenue is ideally positioned within a modern development on the southern edge of Cambridge, offering a rare balance of city convenience and immediate access to open countryside. The property is within half a mile of the Cambridge Biomedical Campus and Addenbrooke’s Hospital, making it particularly well suited to professionals working in the area.
The location is exceptionally well connected, with Cambridge South Station (approximately 0.7 miles) providing fast and regular services to London Liverpool Street, King’s Cross and Stansted Airport. In addition, nearby bus stops at Addenbrooke’s offer excellent links across the city and surrounding areas.

The property also benefits from direct access to the Cambridge Cycle Network, enabling convenient and safe cycling into the city centre and beyond.

A particular feature of this location is its proximity to open green space. Nine Wells Nature Reserve is within a mile, while the Gog Magog Hills and Wandlebury Country Park offer extensive walking and outdoor recreation just a two miles away, creating an attractive setting for those seeking access to nature alongside city living.

Cambridge city centre provides a wide range of cultural and recreational amenities, including the Fitzwilliam Museum, Cambridge University Botanic Garden, Kettle’s Yard, the Arts Theatre and the Corn Exchange. The city also offers a popular daily market at Market Square, along with extensive shopping at the Grand Arcade.

There are a number of highly regarded schools for all age groups in both the state and independent sectors, including The Perse and The Leys, with Hills Road and Long Road Sixth Form Colleges.

All distances and times are approximate

