13 Owlstone Road is believed to date from the early 1900''s and is a fine example of the period with well-proportioned rooms and high ceilings. Built with brick elevations under a slate roof, the property is an attractive and well-positioned period house in the heart of Newnham, one of Cambridge’s most consistently sought-after residential areas. The property has clearly been thoughtfully reconfigured and improved, now providing beautifully presented four-bedroom accommodation. The improvements, including the new kitchen, bathrooms and general presentation, give the house a very appealing “turn-key” quality, The property further benefits from a detached garden studio and would also be offered with the significant benefit of no onward chain.

Owlstone Road lies to the west of the city within the highly regarded Newnham area, widely recognised as one of the best residential locations in the city. Local facilities include a post office, chemist, bakers, butchers, grocers, small supermarket, the highly regarded Newnham Croft Primary School and Lammas Land Recreation Ground, with a large children''s'' play area, tennis court and paddling pool. The property is also situated close to the Paradise Nature Reserve.

The historic city centre is about half a mile away and provides an attractive combination of ancient and modern buildings, colleges, winding lanes and extensive shopping facilities. The property is extremely well placed for many of the University departments, ''The Backs'' and delightful walks along the River Cam to the nearby villages of Grantchester and Coton. There is also an excellent range of schools for all ages within half to three-quarters of a mile of the property, including King''s College School and St John''s College School in Grange Road.', 'Bidwells, Cambridge Sales', '2026-09-08T09:46:33Z', '2026-10-24T10:05:54Z', '[]', 'eval');
