The house provides a really good balance of generous reception space and flexible bedroom accommodation, making it particularly well suited to family life while also offering the versatility increasingly sought by buyers working partly from home.

The ground floor is centred around an excellent sitting and dining room measuring approximately 21`5" x 15`3". It is a wonderfully generous main reception space with room for both substantial seating and a full dining area.

Beyond this an extension provides an additional informal living space which could equally work as a study or playroom.

The kitchen sits separately alongside the main reception accommodation and provides good storage and workspace, while a ground floor WC adds useful practicality.

The first floor provides two particularly generous bedrooms. The principal bedroom measures approximately 15`3" x 10`7", while the second measures approximately 13`2" x 9`11". There are also two bath/shower rooms on this level.

The second floor provides a further three bedrooms, including another excellent double bedroom measuring approximately 15`5" x 11`4", together with a further shower room.

Altogether, the house provides five genuine bedrooms and three bathrooms across the upper floors, giving it a level of accommodation which is increasingly difficult to find this close to central Oxford.

The property has plenty of character internally, with attractive timber flooring, built-in shelving and an established, comfortable feel with the benefit of wonderful views of Castle Mill Stream in the winter months. The reception rooms are particularly appealing, with excellent natural light and a layout that provides separation without compromising the sense of space.

Its combination of approximately 1,662 sq ft, five bedrooms and an extremely central position makes this a particularly compelling option for buyers wanting substantial accommodation without moving further away from the heart of Oxford.

Location

Rewley Road occupies one of Oxford`s most convenient city-centre positions, perfectly balancing connectivity with a surprisingly peaceful waterside setting.

Oxford Railway Station is only a short walk away, providing direct services to London Paddington, Birmingham and the Cotswolds, making this an ideal base for commuters. Oxford city centre, Gloucester Green, the Westgate Shopping Centre and Oxford`s historic colleges are all within comfortable walking distance.

The nearby Oxford Canal provides picturesque towpath walks towards Jericho and Port Meadow, while the vibrant Jericho district offers an excellent selection of independent cafés, restaurants, gastro pubs, boutiques and the renowned Phoenix Picturehouse cinema. The area has long been regarded as one of Oxford`s most desirable neighbourhoods thanks to its unique village atmosphere and attractive canal-side setting.

The property is also exceptionally well placed for Oxford University departments, the Saïd Business School, Oxford Castle Quarter and the city`s extensive cultural, shopping and leisure facilities.

