Designed and built approximately nine years ago as one of just three homes within this discreet mews style development, the property offers a rare combination of space, privacy and modern design. Arranged over four thoughtfully planned floors, the house is filled with natural light and has been finished to an exacting standard, creating a home that feels as impressive in its detail as it is effortless to live in.

At the heart of the property is a beautifully appointed kitchen and dining space, centred around a bespoke handmade kitchen with Corian work surfaces, an induction hob, Quooker hot tap and premium integrated appliances. The adjoining reception room opens through full width tri-fold doors onto a landscaped rear garden, creating an easy connection between the inside and outside and a wonderfully sociable space for entertaining.

All four bedrooms are genuinely well proportioned doubles, with the principal bedroom enjoying its own stylish, fully tiled walk in shower room. The remaining bedrooms are served by a beautifully finished family bathroom with stainless steel fittings and a rainfall shower.

Throughout the house, the emphasis is on intelligent modern living. Underfloor heating runs throughout, allowing the rooms to remain uncluttered, while engineered solid oak flooring brings warmth and texture to the principal living spaces. Large windows maximise the natural light, while an integrated Smart Home system incorporates surround sound, custom lighting and pre installed technology connections for contemporary living.

The accommodation continues on the lower ground floor with an impressive 24ft integrated secure garage. There is a practical utility area and WC, with further potential to tailor the space to suit individual requirements. Outside, the driveway offers further off street parking. A huge bonus not to be overlooked is the end of terrace plot with side access leading directly to the rear garden.

The location is where this home truly comes into its own. Cintra Park is a leafy, tree lined residential street, yet the best of Crystal Palace is quite literally on the doorstep. The Triangle provides the neighbourhood’s unmistakable village like centre, where independent cafés, restaurants, boutiques, bars and specialist shops create a wonderfully sociable atmosphere and a genuine sense of community. Crystal Palace Park is close by, offering acres of open green space, while the station provides convenient connections into central London.

And the area is only becoming more exciting. Crystal Palace is firmly in high demand, with its distinctive blend of period character, green open spaces, independent businesses and excellent transport links continuing to attract buyers looking for something beyond the conventional London neighbourhood. The arrival of much loved names including Gail’s Bakery and Everyman Cinema, alongside further exciting additions to the local scene, is set to add another layer to an already thriving destination.

