Description

Chestnut Lodge is a beautifully presented detached family home, featuring superb reception rooms, a modern kitchen and utility area, underfloor heating and versatile living space, ideal for modern family life and entertaining.

Impressive primary reception areas comprise a spacious triple aspect sitting room with a feature fireplace, a bow window with a view to the front, and bi-fold doors opening to the rear terrace; and an adjoining dining room with a view to the garden and an opening to the kitchen.

A playroom has fitted storage and enjoys a bow window with a view to the front, providing additional reception space if required.

The modern kitchen is fitted with a comprehensive range of sleek wall and base units with integral appliances, with worksurfaces extending to a utility area which provides further storage and space for appliances. Doors open to the side terrace.

A cloakroom and coats cupboard completes the ground floor.

From the welcoming entrance hall stairs rise to the first floor and superb principal bedroom, featuring a dual aspect, built-in storage and a modern en suite shower room.

There are three further bedrooms, all benefitting from fitted wardrobe space and eaves access.

A well-appointed family bathroom and a laundry cupboard complete the accommodation.

Chestnut Lodge is approached over a herringbone brick paved driveway culminating at the detached garaging and providing ample off road parking. There are two detached garages, one with an adjoining outbuilding/gardening store room, providing versatile external space.

The attractive gardens are predominantly laid to landscaped lawn wrapping to the rear and side of the property, interspersed with a variety of established planting including a number of majestic trees. A paved terrace spans the property and provides excellent areas for al fresco entertaining, with a variety of close board fencing, hedging and trees to the perimeter.

Location

27 Larkfield Road is situated on the edge of the popular village of Bessels Green. The adjoining village of Riverhead provides a chemist, butcher, public house, church, library, wine merchants, convenience store, local shops, and a Tesco superstore.

Comprehensive Shopping: Sevenoaks town centre (2.2 miles), Tunbridge Wells (13.2 miles) and Bluewater (15.4 miles).

Mainline Rail Services: Sevenoaks (1.8 miles) to London Bridge (from 22 minutes)/Cannon Street/Charing Cross.

Primary Schools: Chevening, Riverhead and Amherst CP Schools. Various in Sevenoaks including Sevenoaks CP, St Thomas'' RCP, St John''s CEP and Lady Boswell''s CEP Schools.

Secondary Schools: Judd Boys Grammar, Weald of Kent and Tonbridge Girls Grammars in Tonbridge. Knole Academy, Weald of Kent Girls & Tunbridge Wells Boys Grammar annexes and Trinity Schools in Sevenoaks.

Private Schools: Sevenoaks, Tonbridge, Sackville and Walthamstow Hall Public Schools. Sevenoaks, Solefields, The Granville and New Beacon Preparatory Schools in Sevenoaks. St Michaels & Russell House Preparatory Schools in Otford. Radnor House in Sundridge.

Leisure Facilities: Sailing and water sports on Chipstead Lake, tennis at Chipstead village club together with football and cricket clubs. Wildernesse and Knole Golf Clubs in Sevenoaks. Nizels Golf and Leisure Centre in Hildenborough. Sevenoaks Swimming and Leisure Centre. Cricket, hockey, football and rugby in the Sevenoaks Vine area. A network of footpaths in the area.

Please note that all distances, timings and measurements are approximate.

Square Footage: 1,708 sq ft

Directions

From Sevenoaks, head north on the London Road to Riverhead, passing the station on your left. At the roundabout in Riverhead take the first exit onto the A25 towards the Westerham and the M25. Continue along this road for about 0.7 miles before turning left into Bessels Way, just along from The Kings Head public house. Turn right into Larkfield Road and the shared driveway leading to No. 27 can be found along on the right hand side.

Additional Info

