A Beautifully Positioned Country Home with Equestrian Facilities, Far-Reaching South Downs Views & Exceptional Flexibility

Originally built in 1925, Conifers occupies a wonderfully private and elevated position along a quiet rural lane, enjoying far-reaching views across the surrounding open countryside within the South Downs National Park.

Discreetly tucked away yet exceptionally well connected, the property offers the rare combination of rural tranquillity and accessibility, with convenient access to the A23 and A27 providing excellent connections towards Brighton, the coast and beyond.

The accommodation has been thoughtfully arranged to provide a versatile and contemporary family home, whilst retaining an appealing blend of character and individuality. Of particular note is the generous kitchen and living space, centred around a charming Victorian log-burning stove set within a brick-built hearth beneath a handsome bressumer beam. The room provides an exceptional setting for both everyday family life and entertaining, with ample space for a substantial dining table and the potential to reinstate the original expansive open-plan arrangement.

A welcoming entrance hall leads to a beautifully presented utility room and WC, formerly the third bedroom and offering the straightforward possibility of reinstatement if required.

The principal bedroom suite is a particularly impressive space, with polished concrete flooring, skylights flooding the room with natural light and double doors opening directly onto a private sunken patio. The adjoining ensuite bathroom has been beautifully appointed with a freestanding roll-top bath, walk-in shower, wash hand basin and WC.

The study is an exceptionally light and attractive room, enjoying delightful garden views through an original large bay window, complemented by useful built-in cupboards.

A further reception room is accessed from the kitchen/living room and benefits from its own independent entrance, offering considerable flexibility and potential for annexe accommodation, guest accommodation or independent living. The room incorporates a fitted kitchen area, polished concrete flooring, contemporary log-burning stove and generous open-plan space for dining and relaxation.

Bi-fold doors open into a superb glazed family room, creating a wonderful connection between the house and gardens. Skylights enhance the sense of space and light, whilst sliding doors provide seamless access onto the patio and garden beyond.

Bedroom Two enjoys direct access to the garden and is complemented by a dressing room and adjacent bathroom, providing an ideal private suite for family members or guests.

OUTSIDE

The approach to Conifers is particularly impressive, with a five-bar gate opening onto a sweeping circular driveway, providing extensive parking and creating an impressive sense of arrival.

A bespoke, fully fitted laundry room provides excellent practical storage, with an array of built-in cupboards and additional worktop space, conveniently positioned alongside the garage. The driveway continues beyond the main house through a further five-bar gate, leading directly to the stable yard and equestrian facilities.

The gardens wrap around the property and are predominantly laid to lawn, bordered by mature trees, established hedging and a variety of fruit trees, creating a wonderfully private and established setting.

The equestrian facilities comprise three stables and a tack room, together with three additional garden stores and a substantial timber outbuilding. A winding pathway leads through to the sand school and adjoining paddocks, all enclosed by traditional post-and-rail fencing.

The grounds are enhanced by mature trees and established hedging, incorporating an ancient orchard, greenhouse and productive vegetable garden, together with an extensive selection of fruit trees which provide year-round interest and seasonal colour.

To the rear of the house, an extensive paved terrace wraps around the property, creating an exceptional area for outdoor dining and entertaining. A discreetly positioned hot tub/swim spa provides the perfect private retreat from which to relax and enjoy the peaceful surroundings.

ENERGY EFFICIENCY & SUSTAINABILITY

Conifers benefits from a comprehensive range of modern energy-efficient features, including solar panels with battery storage, an air source heat pump and underfloor heating throughout. An EV smart charging point is also conveniently positioned by the garage.

A UNIQUE COUNTRY HOME

Conifers presents a rare opportunity to acquire a private and characterful country residence with excellent equestrian facilities, generous gardens and grounds, flexible accommodation and far-reaching countryside views.

The combination of its elevated South Downs National Park setting, exceptional outdoor facilities, adaptable living accommodation and excellent transport connections makes Conifers a truly distinctive rural home.', 'Batcheller Monkhouse, Pulborough', '2026-09-29T15:01:03Z', '2026-10-24T10:04:48Z', '[]', 'train');

Conceived by the architects as a spliced modern insertion within a Victorian vernacular, the house has been comprehensively remodelled by the present owners. The end of terrace position presented a rare opportunity to extend both widthways and lengthways, creating an unusually spacious home. The result is a compelling contrast between the original Victorian building and the bold industrial character of the rear addition.

At its heart is an impressive open plan kitchen, dining and family space, formed through the replacement of the original ground floor kitchen outrigger with a light filled extension. Soaring ceilings, expansive glazing and a polished microcement floors create a dramatic sense of light and volume, while large glazed doors open directly onto the garden, providing a seamless connection between the interior and outside space.

Exposed steel elements are celebrated in dramatic tones, clearly defining the junction between the original building and the new extension. The material palette has a raw, earthy quality, with limewash paints and natural oil finishes complementing the Oxford red brick walls and natural slate roof. Double doors connect the kitchen with a more intimate bay fronted sitting room, where original pine floorboards and a sleek real flame gas fire introduce warmth and character.

On the first floor are two well proportioned double bedrooms and a dramatic family bathroom with a freestanding bath, separate shower and vaulted ceiling. The principal bedroom suite occupies the entire second floor and includes an en suite shower room and Juliet balcony overlooking the rear garden.

The property is approached via a paved pathway, with a small front garden providing practical space for bicycles and bins. To the rear is an attractive walled garden, thoughtfully landscaped with raised beds surrounding a central lawn and a paved terrace positioned at the far end.

East Avenue is a sought after no through road running between Cowley Road and Morrell Avenue, offering convenient access to central Oxford and the area’s excellent selection of independent shops, cafés, bars and restaurants. South Park, Oxford Brookes University and a range of well regarded schools are all within walking distance, while frequent coach services provide direct connections to London Victoria, Heathrow, Gatwick and Stansted airports.', 'Scottfraser, East Oxford', '2026-09-29T15:16:02Z', '2026-10-24T10:54:57Z', '["floor_level"]', 'eval');

