At the opposite end of the reception is the contemporary kitchen, which also benefits from excellent natural light through large areas of glazing and a door opening onto the front terrace. Sleek, handleless white cabinetry is paired with contrasting light grey worktops, creating a clean and modern finish. Integrated appliances, including a wine fridge, are neatly incorporated into the design, while the generous open-plan arrangement ensures the kitchen remains connected to the dining and living areas.

Stairs lead to the upper floor, where two well-proportioned double bedrooms are positioned alongside two bathrooms. The principal bedroom is particularly well equipped, benefiting from a range of built-in wardrobes providing excellent storage and a stylish en-suite bathroom with a walk-in shower. The second double bedroom is also generously sized and benefits from natural light, while further useful storage can be found within the hallway.

The family bathroom is finished in a contemporary style, featuring a deep bathtub with handheld shower, grey wall tiling and contrasting floor tiling. The well-planned arrangement of the accommodation ensures the bedrooms feel comfortably separated from the main living space.

The location is ideally suited to those wanting to make the most of both Clapham and Brixton. Clapham High Street is moments away, offering an extensive selection of restaurants, bars, cafés and shops, while Venn Street provides a popular local destination for food and weekend markets. Clapham Common is also within easy reach, providing plenty of open green space. Clapham North Underground station is close by, offering access to the Northern Line, with Clapham High Street Overground also nearby. Brixton is within walking distance, providing access to the Victoria Line, Brixton Village, the Ritzy Cinema and an extensive choice of independent shops, restaurants and bars.', 'Keating Estates, Balham', '2026-09-30T10:54:36Z', '2026-10-23T22:54:28Z', '[]', 'train');

