The Home

Established planting screens the front garden, setting the house back from the pavement and providing a green outlook from the reception room.

The entrance hallway keeps the staircase separate from the living accommodation, with storage and a downstairs WC arranged beyond. The through lounge runs from the curved front bay towards the kitchen at the rear. White walls, decorative cornicing and a fireplace give this room a restrained character, while its open connection with the kitchen allows the downstairs accommodation to work as one connected space.

Across the rear of the house, the kitchen has pale cabinetry against exposed brick walls, with rooflights bringing daylight into the room from above. There is space for a dining table alongside the cooking area, and black-framed French doors open onto the garden. A further run of cabinetry and worktop extends back towards the hallway, adding useful preparation and storage space away from the main dining area.

All three bedrooms sit together on the first floor. Two larger rooms face the front and rear respectively, while the smaller front bedroom could also serve as a nursery or study. The family bathroom has a bath with an overhead shower, white wall tiles and patterned floor tiles. Double glazing is fitted throughout the house.

Outside, the rear garden is arranged with paved areas, a central lawn, raised beds and established boundary planting. Steps divide the different levels, giving space for outdoor seating as well as planting. A separate external store provides additional storage without taking space from the house.

Planning permission was granted in June 2022 for a loft conversion with a rear dormer, three front rooflights and enlargement of a rear first-floor bedroom window, reference HGY/2022/1284. This has since lapsed.

The Neighbourhood

Quernmore Road has its own small cluster of independent businesses near Harringay station. But First, Coffee provides a local stop for coffee and pastries, while Bonne Route offers wine and small plates on the same street.
For eating out, The Goods Office on Ferme Park Road serves food throughout the day, and Pizzeria Pappagone on Stroud Green Road is an established option for pizza and Italian cooking. Across towards Green Lanes, The Dusty Knuckle adds another bakery and café, with evening pizza sessions too. Everyday shopping includes Tesco Superstore and Sainsbury''s Local on Stroud Green Road.

Stationers Park provides nearby green space, while local primary schools include St Aidan''s on Albany Road and Weston Park Primary School.

Harringay station provides Great Northern services towards Moorgate. Harringay Green Lanes offers a separate connection to London Overground''s Suffragette line, giving useful alternatives for journeys across London.

