An impressive three/four-bedroom 1930s family home, offering over 1,400 sq ft of beautifully presented and highly versatile accommodation - perfectly blending period character with stylish contemporary living.

The property makes an immediate impression with its handsome double-bay façade and superb kerb appeal, while the interior continues to impress with a high-quality finish throughout. A fine selection of modern, high-specification fixtures and fittings sits comfortably alongside a wealth of original-style character, including towering ceilings, elegant cornicing, ceiling roses and feature fireplaces.

At the heart of the home is the stunning open-plan kitchen/dining space, thoughtfully designed to create a wonderful hub for everyday family life. Generous proportions and a sociable layout make this the ideal setting for everything from relaxed breakfasts and family dinners to entertaining friends and hosting special occasions.

For quieter moments, the large separate front reception room provides an inviting retreat, with the attractive bay window and period detailing creating an elegant yet comfortable space in which to relax.

The first floor offers three generously proportioned bedrooms together with a beautifully appointed luxury family bathroom. A further staircase rises to the converted loft, providing an impressive and highly versatile additional room, currently utilised as an unofficial fourth bedroom, but equally well suited to a home office, guest room or teenager''s retreat

Outside, the beautifully presented rear garden provides the perfect extension of the living space. Predominantly laid to lawn and complemented by a patio area, mature trees and established shrubs, it offers a delightful setting for children''s play, alfresco dining, summer entertaining or simply relaxing outdoors.

Combining generous living space, period charm, contemporary style and excellent versatility, this is a superb family home with an abundance of personality and a layout perfectly suited to modern-day living.

Location
Oak Hill Gardens occupies an enviable position on the borders of Woodford Green, South Woodford and Walthamstow, providing residents with the best of both worlds: a wonderfully green, residential setting combined with excellent access to the shops, restaurants, transport links and amenities of this sought-after part of East London. The road itself is a peaceful cul-de-sac, with Epping Forest just moments away, while both South Woodford and Highams Park are within easy reach.

One of the area''s greatest attractions is its outstanding access to green space and the outdoors. The ancient woodland of Epping Forest is practically on the doorstep, providing a fantastic natural playground for walking, running, cycling and weekend adventures. Highams Park Lake is another popular local destination, offering an attractive setting for leisurely walks and time outdoors. For buyers who want the convenience of London life without sacrificing greenery, it is a particularly compelling location.

Commuters are well catered for, with a choice of transport options available from the surrounding neighbourhoods. South Woodford provides access to the Central line, creating a convenient route towards Stratford, Liverpool Street and the West End, while Highams Park offers London Overground services towards Liverpool Street. The wider location also provides straightforward access towards Woodford, Walthamstow and the North Circular, making Oak Hill Gardens well placed for those travelling both into and around London.

Everyday amenities are plentiful. Residents can take advantage of the shops, cafés, restaurants and services found throughout Woodford Green and South Woodford, together with the increasingly vibrant collection of independent businesses around Highams Park. Local favourites highlighted in the area include The Stag & Lantern and Vino Tap, helping to give the neighbourhood an appealing independent feel. Walthamstow is also easily accessible, offering an even broader choice of shopping, dining and leisure facilities.

For families, the wider Woodford, Highams Park and Walthamstow area offers an established selection of primary and secondary schools, alongside nurseries and childcare facilities. This, combined with the quiet residential surroundings and exceptional access to Epping Forest, makes the location particularly attractive to buyers looking to put down longer-term roots.

Ultimately, Oak Hill Gardens offers a lifestyle that can be difficult to find so close to central London: peaceful residential surroundings, vast expanses of woodland and green space, excellent local amenities and convenient commuter connections. Its position between Woodford Green, South Woodford, Highams Park and Walthamstow means residents can enjoy the individual character and facilities of several popular neighbourhoods, while coming home to the tranquillity of a leafy setting beside Epping Forest.

Why this works for an advert: The emphasis is deliberately on the strongest buyer motivations for this location: Epping Forest, connectivity, family appeal, amenities and the ability to enjoy several neighbouring areas rather than being restricted to one town centre.

